        "description": "**About The Company**\n Sierra is a pioneering technology company dedicated to transforming customer experiences through the power of artificial intelligence. With a focus on building innovative platforms, Sierra collaborates with industry leaders such as SoftBank, Uber, Rivian, CLEAR, and Sutter Health to create solutions that are both impactful and user\\-centric. Headquartered in San Francisco, Sierra maintains a strong in\\-person presence while expanding its offices across North America, Europe, and Asia. The company's culture is rooted in core values including Trust, Customer Obsession, Craftsmanship, Intensity, and Family, which guide every aspect of its operations and employee engagement. Founded by renowned industry veterans Bret Taylor and Clay Bavor, Sierra benefits from their extensive experience in technology and product leadership, including roles at Google, Facebook, Salesforce, and OpenAI. Bret Taylor currently serves as Board Chair of OpenAI, bringing a wealth of expertise in AI and product development, while Clay Bavor's leadership in Google Labs and AR/VR initiatives underscores Sierra's commitment to cutting\\-edge innovation.\n   \n\n  \n\n**About The Role**\n We are seeking a talented Frontend Developer to join Sierra’s dynamic team. In this role, you will be instrumental in shaping the user experience across our core product interfaces and marketing platforms. Your work will directly impact how users interact with Sierra’s solutions, ensuring a seamless, engaging, and accessible experience. You will own the development of frontend features, collaborate closely with cross\\-functional teams including marketing, design, and content, and help build scalable content infrastructure. Additionally, you will champion performance optimization and accessibility standards, ensuring our digital presence is fast, reliable, and inclusive. This position offers a unique opportunity to contribute to a rapidly growing company at the forefront of AI innovation, impacting a global audience through thoughtful and user\\-focused web development.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Qualifications**\n The ideal candidate will possess a blend of technical expertise, growth mindset, and collaborative spirit. You should have a solid foundation in modern frontend development, including proficiency in JavaScript, TypeScript, and React or similar frameworks. Experience working with headless CMS platforms like Sanity is highly desirable. A strong understanding of performance optimization, accessibility standards, and internationalization is essential. You should be familiar with marketing and growth\\-related metrics such as funnels, SEO, and A/B testing, demonstrating an understanding of how technical decisions influence business outcomes. Excellent communication skills and the ability to work effectively with non\\-engineering teams—such as designers, content creators, and marketers—are critical. A track record of integrating third\\-party services and working with structured content models will be considered a plus. Candidates with experience in localization, analytics, experimentation, and content workflows will stand out.\n   \n\n  \n\n**Responsibilities**\n* Own the development and maintenance of frontend interfaces across Sierra’s core product and marketing platforms, ensuring a cohesive and polished user experience. Collaborate with design and product teams to implement features that are both functional and visually appealing.\n* Develop and enhance content infrastructure by designing schemas and editing experiences within our CMS (Sanity), enabling content and marketing teams to manage content independently and efficiently without reliance on engineering support.\n* Partner with marketing, sales, and operations teams to implement analytics tracking and experimentation frameworks. Translate business objectives into measurable features, enabling data\\-driven decision\\-making and continuous optimization.\n* Support localization and internationalization efforts by developing multilingual content workflows, translation management, and infrastructure to ensure a first\\-class experience for users worldwide.\n* Prioritize performance as a core feature by owning Core Web Vitals, media optimization, and diagnosing subtle issues like layout shifts, lazy\\-loading inefficiencies, and render timing. Measure and improve site speed continuously.\n* Champion accessibility best practices, including semantic markup, keyboard navigation, screen\\-reader support, and WCAG compliance, to ensure the platform is usable by everyone.\n\n\n**Benefits**\n Sierra is committed to supporting its employees with a comprehensive benefits package that reflects its core values. Full\\-time employees enjoy flexible (unlimited) paid time off, enabling work\\-life balance. The company provides robust medical, dental, and vision coverage for employees and their families, along with life insurance and disability benefits. Retirement plans are available depending on regional policies, and parental leave policies support new parents. Sierra also offers fertility and family\\-building benefits through Carrot, along with daily amenities such as lunch, snacks, and coffee to foster a productive environment. Employees receive a discretionary stipend to spend on personal priorities and enjoy unique perks like free alphorn lessons. These benefits are designed to promote well\\-being, professional growth, and a supportive workplace culture.\n   \n\n  \n\n Equal Opportunity\n   \n\n  \n\n Sierra is an equal opportunity employer dedicated to fostering an inclusive environment where all employees and applicants are treated with respect and fairness. The company values diversity in skills, backgrounds, and perspectives, believing that a varied team enhances innovation and creativity. Sierra encourages candidates from all backgrounds to apply, regardless of race, color, religion, gender, gender identity or expression, sexual orientation, national origin, age, disability, veteran status, or any other protected class. The company is committed to providing accommodations for individuals with disabilities and ensuring a welcoming, supportive environment for everyone.",
